{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-ns-singularity-descartes","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:ns-singularity-descartes","kind":"theorem","title":"Topology of the Reeb bundle of the Descartes universe","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-qu-to-qou"],"tags":["theorem","navier-stokes","descartes","categorical"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.FluidDynamics.descartes_kummer_root_levels","text":"ns-singularity-descartes.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:ns-singularity-descartes\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be the Descartes quantum universe, with base Bring's surface <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}</code> of genus <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\chi(\\mathcal{S}) = \\chi_{\\mathrm{eu}}(M_0) = -6</code>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code> be its Reeb <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{U}(1)</code>-bundle, the unit tangent bundle of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}</code>. Then:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e(\\xi) = c_1(\\xi) = -6 \\in H^2(\\mathcal{S}, \\mathbb{Z}) \\cong \\mathbb{Z}</code>. In particular <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code> has no nowhere-vanishing section.</li>\n<li>For <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n \\geq 1</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code> has an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code>-th root if and only if <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n \\in \\{1, 2, 3, 6\\}</code>. For every other <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> the obstruction <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-6 \\bmod n \\in H^2(\\mathcal{S}, \\mu_n) \\cong \\mathbb{Z}/n</code> is non-zero.</li>\n<li>For any one-dimensional locus <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Sigma \\subset \\mathcal{S}</code>, the restriction of each of these classes to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Sigma</code> is zero, since <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H^2(\\Sigma, \\cdot) = 0</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-singularity-descartes.md","heading":"Theorem","number":"20.6.8","page":"b/thm-ns-singularity-descartes","qa":{"counts":{"pass":89,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":74},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.FluidDynamics.ns_singularity_descartes.descartes_kummer_root_levels","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/ns_singularity_descartes.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
